{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786481691,"nonce":"eepabIV2bxEy8EUpp61tmCmUMyg=","title":"**What is wrong.** The per-silence Alertmanager deep link is threaded through the whole silences HTTP layer as a constructor parameter, a router field and a nullable DTO field — and the composition root supplies it as a literal empty string. `internal/app/container.go:918`:","message":"```go\nfunc (c *Container) alertmanagerURL() string { return \"\" }\n```\n\nIt is called at `internal/app/container.go:898` and nowhere else. There is no config key behind it, no environment variable, no per-source lookup. `SilenceDTO.AlertmanagerURL` (`internal/silences/api/dto.go:44`) is therefore `null` in every response oto has ever served in production.\n\n**The demonstration.** `internal/silences/api/silences.go:52-56` takes the value and trims it onto `Router.alertmanagerURL`; `:211-215` is the only consumer:\n\n```go\nif rt.alertmanagerURL == \"\" {\n\treturn nil\n}\nurl := rt.alertmanagerURL + \"/#/silences/\" + s.SourceSilenceID()\n```\n\nThe only non-empty value anywhere in the tree is `contractAlertmanagerURL = \"https://alertmanager.example.com\"` at `internal/silences/api/silences_contract_test.go:53`, passed to `NewRouter` at `:204`. The link is exercised exclusively by a test.\n\nCONTEXT.md §4 marks `silences` as *\"PERIPHERAL | Read-only mirror of AM silences. **No write path.**\"*, which makes this deep link the module's entire outward affordance: v1 cannot create, extend or expire a silence, so sending the operator to the Alertmanager UI is all it can offer. `deepLink`'s own comment at `:206-209` argues correctly that *\"A guessed link is worse than none: an operator who clicks it during an incident and lands on a 404 has lost the one affordance v1 offers\"* — but the branch it guards is the only branch that ever runs.\n\nThe shape is also wrong for the product. One process-wide URL cannot serve an N-source deployment: a silence belongs to a source (`Silence.SourceID()`, `internal/silences/domain/silence.go:250`, already rendered as `SourceID` in the DTO at `internal/silences/api/silences.go:190`), and `sources.domain.Source` already carries `BaseURL` (`internal/sources/domain/source.go:83-85`). Even if the container returned a configured value, it would deep-link every silence from every cluster to the same Alertmanager, and for all but one source that is precisely the 404 the comment warns about.\n\n`tools/lintreach` cannot see this. Its `noread` check fires on a struct field with zero production reads, and `Router.alertmanagerURL` is read twice at `:211` and `:214`; its `nowrite` check sees the keyed composite-literal write at `:56`. The constant is on the write side of a live field, which is a shape none of the three checks model.\n\n**Why it matters.** The only affordance the silences feature has is dead in every deployment, and it is dead in the way that is hardest to notice: the field is present in the contract, the code path exists, a contract test covers it, and the value is `null` because a function in the composition root returns a literal. Nothing fails. An operator reads `\"alertmanager_url\": null` and concludes oto could not determine the link, when in fact oto never tries.\n\n**Where.** `internal/app/container.go:915-918` (the hardwired `\"\"` and its comment), `:898` (the only call), `internal/silences/api/silences.go:44-48,52-56,201,206-215`, `internal/silences/api/dto.go:44`, `internal/silences/api/silences_contract_test.go:53,204` (the only non-empty value), `internal/silences/domain/silence.go:250` and `internal/sources/domain/source.go:83-85` (the per-source data the link should derive from).\n\n**Scope.** small\n\n**Done when.** The deep link either derives from the silence's own source — `Silence.SourceID()` resolving to that `Source.BaseURL` — or the parameter, the router field, the `deepLink` method and the DTO field are all removed together. `alertmanagerURL()` returning a literal is gone either way.","files":null}]}